llation, only diff is that it has all known collections\n\u003e    registered.\n\njust for my education: wouldn't then the entire website be ran by\ncherrypy, or we would just use it as cgi?\n\n## \n\nYaroslav O. Halchenko, Ph.D.\nhttp://neuro.debian.net http://www.pymvpa.org http://www.fail2ban.org\nResearch Scientist,            Psychological and Brain Sciences Dept.\nDartmouth College, 419 Moore Hall, Hinman Box 6207, Hanover, NH 03755\nPhone: +1 (603) 646-9834                       Fax: +1 (603) 646-1419\nWWW:   http://www.linkedin.com/in/yarik","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1435076653,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDExNDU2MjQ2NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/168#issuecomment-114562465"},"message":"The webSITE would not.\n\nMy concept is this: There is a webSERVICE running somewhere. The webSITE can query that SERVICE with some javascript in order to list collections or resolve other search queries. The same SERVICE can be queried by datalad installation in order to obtain information on available collections (maybe even other things).\n\nBut it really should be a thin shell around a datalad installation. The size of the DB or sluggishness of responses could force us to switch to a dedicated triple store (eventually/optionally). However, when this happens, it must not be different from the use case of a regular user-side datalad installation that has to deal with LOTS of collections/handles.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474380831,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI0ODMxMzU0Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/168#issuecomment-248313542"},"message":"we have the index now, the rest is for separate discussions etc","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1474380832,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3